WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.313
A connected server is
addressable, not yet governed.

2
00:00:03.313 --> 00:00:05.787
Attach three things on the same change.

3
00:00:05.787 --> 00:00:11.074
Govern with Azure machine configuration,
formerly Azure Policy Guest Configuration.

4
00:00:11.074 --> 00:00:15.735
It extends Azure Policy inside the
operating system, using Desired State

5
00:00:15.735 --> 00:00:20.700
Configuration to audit or set OS settings,
and reports compliance per machine.

6
00:00:20.700 --> 00:00:24.725
Unlike Group Policy it's scoped
by Azure resource scope,

7
00:00:24.725 --> 00:00:28.312
subscription, resource
group or machine, not by OU.

8
00:00:28.312 --> 00:00:32.887
The agent includes the service natively,
so there's no extension to deploy.

9
00:00:32.887 --> 00:00:37.876
The Windows and Linux audit baselines are
built-in definitions against the Azure

10
00:00:37.876 --> 00:00:40.737
compute security baseline,
both customizable,

11
00:00:40.737 --> 00:00:44.038
and a CIS benchmark definition
for Linux is in preview.

12
00:00:44.038 --> 00:00:46.744
Deploy the prerequisite initiative first,

13
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:51.555
keep the customized baseline in the
governance repository as policy-as-code,

14
00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:55.388
and treat noncompliance as a
finding, not a failed deployment.

15
00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:57.513
Patch with Azure Update Manager.

16
00:00:57.513 --> 00:01:01.523
It assesses every twenty-four hours
when periodic assessment is on,

17
00:01:01.523 --> 00:01:06.536
patches in maintenance windows, and groups
machines by tag through dynamic scoping,

18
00:01:06.536 --> 00:01:09.400
which is where the patch
group tag earns its keep.

19
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.652
It's charged per Arc server per month,

20
00:01:11.652 --> 00:01:15.030
except when the server is
enabled for ESUs through Arc,

21
00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.634
when Defender for Servers Plan
2 covers the subscription,

22
00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:22.763
or with Software Assurance, a
subscription or pay-as-you-go license.

23
00:01:22.763 --> 00:01:24.825
Protect with Defender for Servers.

24
00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:30.006
Plan 1 centers on endpoint detection and
response; Plan 2 adds agentless scanning,

25
00:01:30.006 --> 00:01:33.816
regulatory compliance, premium
vulnerability management,

26
00:01:33.816 --> 00:01:37.550
configuration assessment and
file integrity monitoring.

27
00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.950
The program's FedRAMP
Moderate scope uses Plan 2,

28
00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.350
plus Defender for SQL on
Arc-connected SQL hosts.

29
00:01:44.350 --> 00:01:48.035
Onboard through Arc rather than
installing Defender directly,

30
00:01:48.035 --> 00:01:49.912
which gives only Plan 1 function.

31
00:01:49.912 --> 00:01:54.002
And if your only Defender entitlement
comes through Defender for Servers,

32
00:01:54.002 --> 00:01:56.640
security settings
management isn't available.
